<% content_for :title, "Governance — Omarchy Plugins" %>
<section class="terminal-page">
  <article class="terminal-window terminal-window--ansi" aria-labelledby="governance-title">
    <%= render "shared/terminal_window_header", title: "Governance",
          route_alias: "learn.governance", status: "read only", command: "omarchy registry powers", cursor: false %>

    <div class="terminal-window__layout">
      <nav class="terminal-window__index terminal-window__index--tree" aria-label="Governance sections"
           data-controller="terminal-tree">
        <div class="terminal-window__index-inner">
          <b>Tree ./governance</b>
          <div class="terminal-window__tree">
            <%= link_to "#powers", class: "is-active", aria: { current: "location" },
                  data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├─</span><span>powers</span>
            <% end %>
            <%= link_to "#appeals", data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├─</span><span>appeals</span>
            <% end %>
            <%= link_to "#transparency", data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">└─</span><span>transparency</span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </nav>

      <div class="terminal-window__main">
        <h1 id="governance-title">Who can pull the levers.</h1>
        <p class="terminal-window__lede">What you install is what was reviewed. If something malicious slips through, every intervention has a named owner and a public record.</p>

        <section id="powers" class="terminal-section" aria-labelledby="powers-title">
          <h2 id="powers-title" class="terminal-section__title terminal-section__title--plain"><span aria-hidden="true">$ </span>omarchy registry powers</h2>
          <ol class="terminal-actions">
            <li><i aria-hidden="true">[1]</i><b>quarantine</b><span>Freeze a version pending investigation. New installs stop within minutes; bytes remain available for review.</span></li>
            <li><i aria-hidden="true">[2]</i><b>yank / takedown</b><span>Remove a version from resolution permanently. Its name and version remain burned.</span></li>
            <li><i aria-hidden="true">[3]</i><b>kill-bit</b><span>Add an entry to <code>revocations.json</code>, disabling already-installed copies.</span></li>
            <li><i aria-hidden="true">[4]</i><b>publisher revocation</b><span>Suspend a compromised or malicious publisher account.</span></li>
          </ol>
          <div class="terminal-status">
            <b>[ roster pending ]</b>
            <p>The admin roster will appear here by name, together with the holder and storage model of the index-signing key. The page ships before the registry accepts its first outside publisher.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="terminal-note-grid">
          <section id="appeals" class="terminal-note">
            <h2>Appeals</h2>
            <p>Disputed actions go to <a href="mailto:registry@omarchy.org">registry@omarchy.org</a> and receive a public human response.</p>
          </section>
          <section id="transparency" class="terminal-note">
            <h2>Transparency</h2>
            <p>The index is static, signed, and mirrorable. Every administrative action lands in the <%= link_to "public audit log →", audit_log_path %></p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</section>
